<article class="env-lemma" id="02VX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02VX">Lemma <span data-tag="02VX">35.35.2</span>.</a> Let $h : S' \to S$ be a surjective, flat morphism of schemes. The base change functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathit{Sch}/S \longrightarrow \mathit{Sch}/S', \quad X \longmapsto S' \times _ S X  \]
</div>
  <p> is faithful. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $X_1$, $X_2$ be schemes over $S$. Let $\alpha , \beta : X_2 \to X_1$ be morphisms over $S$. If $\alpha $, $\beta $ base change to the same morphism then we get a commutative diagram as follows 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X_2 \ar[d]^\alpha &  S' \times _ S X_2 \ar[l] \ar[d] \ar[r] &  X_2 \ar[d]^\beta \\  X_1 &  S' \times _ S X_1 \ar[l] \ar[r] &  X_1 }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Hence it suffices to show that $S' \times _ S X_2 \to X_2$ is an epimorphism. As the base change of a surjective and flat morphism it is surjective and flat (see Morphisms, Lemmas <a href="/tag/01S1" data-tag="01S1">29.9.4</a> and <a href="/tag/01U9" data-tag="01U9">29.26.8</a>). Hence the lemma follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/02VW" data-tag="02VW">35.35.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>